  "issue_title": "Azure Block Blob credentials are exposed by celery report and configuration sanitization",
  "issue_body": "<!--\nPlease fill this template entirely and do not erase parts of it.\nWe reserve the right to close without a response\nbug reports which are incomplete.\n-->\n\n# Checklist\n\n<!--\nTo check an item on the list replace [ ] with [x].\n-->\n\n* [x] I have verified that the issue exists against the `main` branch of Celery.\n* [ ] This has already been asked to the [[discussions forum](https://github.com/celery/celery/discussions)](https://github.com/celery/celery/discussions) first.\n* [x] I have read the relevant section in the\n  [[contribution guide](https://docs.celeryq.dev/en/main/contributing.html#other-bugs)](https://docs.celeryq.dev/en/main/contributing.html#other-bugs)\n  on reporting bugs.\n* [x] I have checked the [[issues list](https://github.com/celery/celery/issues?q=is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Issue+Type%3A+Bug+Report%22+-label%3A%22Category%3A+Documentation%22)](https://github.com/celery/celery/issues?q=is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Issue+Type%3A+Bug+Report%22+-label%3A%22Category%3A+Documentation%22)\n  for similar or identical bug reports.\n* [x] I have checked the [[pull requests list](https://github.com/celery/celery/pulls?q=is%3Apr+label%3A%22PR+Type%3A+Bugfix%22+-label%3A%22Category%3A+Documentation%22)](https://github.com/celery/celery/pulls?q=is%3Apr+label%3A%22PR+Type%3A+Bugfix%22+-label%3A%22Category%3A+Documentation%22)\n  for existing proposed fixes.\n* [x] I have checked the [[commit log](https://github.com/celery/celery/commits/main)](https://github.com/celery/celery/commits/main)\n  to find out if the bug was already fixed in the main branch.\n* [x] I have included all related issues and possible duplicate issues\n  in this issue (If there are none, check this box anyway).\n* [ ] I have tried to reproduce the issue with [[pytest-celery](https://docs.celeryq.dev/projects/pytest-celery/en/latest/userguide/celery-bug-report.html)](https://docs.celeryq.dev/projects/pytest-celery/en/latest/userguide/celery-bug-report.html) and added the reproduction script below.\n\n## Mandatory Debugging Information\n\n* [x] I have included the output of `celery -A proj report` in the issue.\n  (if you are not able to do this, then at least specify the Celery\n  version affected).\n* [x] I have verified that the issue exists against the `main` branch of Celery.\n* [ ] I have included the contents of `pip freeze` in the issue.\n* [x] I have included all the versions of all the external dependencies required\n  to reproduce this bug.\n\n## Optional Debugging Information\n\n<!--\nTry some of the below if you think they are relevant.\nIt will help us figure out the scope of the bug and how many users it affects.\n-->\n\n* [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one Python version\n  and/or implementation.\n* [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one message broker and/or\n  result backend.\n* [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one version of the message\n  broker and/or result backend.\n* [x] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one operating system.\n* [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue on more than one workers pool.\n* [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue with autoscaling, retries,\n  ETA/Countdown & rate limits disabled.\n* [ ] I have tried reproducing the issue after downgrading\n  and/or upgrading Celery and its dependencies.\n\n## Related Issues and Possible Duplicates\n\n<!--\nPlease make sure to search and mention any related issues\nor possible duplicates to this issue as requested by the checklist above.\n\nThis may or may not include issues in other repositories that the Celery project\nmaintains or other repositories that are dependencies of Celery.\n\nIf you don't know how to mention issues, please refer to Github's documentation\non the subject: https://help.github.com/en/articles/autolinked-references-and-urls#issues-and-pull-requests\n-->\n\n#### Related Issues\n\n* #10620 \u2014 related Azure Block Blob credential redaction fix in `AzureBlockBlobBackend.as_uri()`.\n\n#### Possible Duplicates\n\n* None found.\n\n## Environment & Settings\n\n<!-- Include the contents of celery --version below -->\n\n**Celery version**: `main` (current upstream source)\n\n<!-- Include the output of celery -A proj report below -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>celery report</code> Output:</b></summary>\n<p>\n\n```\nsoftware -> celery:main kombu:... py:3.13.15\n            billiard:... py-amqp:... \nplatform -> system:... arch:...\n            kernel version:...\n            python:3.13.15\n            implementation:CPython\nloader   -> celery.loaders.app.AppLoader\nsettings -> broker_url:...\n            result_backend:azureblockblob://DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=acct;AccountKey=SECRET==;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net\n            ...\n```\n\n</p>\n</details>\n\n# Steps to Reproduce\n\n## Required Dependencies\n\n<!-- Please fill the required dependencies to reproduce this issue -->\n\n* **Minimal Python Version**: Python 3.13\n* **Minimal Celery Version**: Current `main`\n* **Minimal Kombu Version**: Current version from `main` environment\n* **Minimal Broker Version**: Not relevant; reproduction uses the in-memory broker\n* **Minimal Result Backend Version**: Azure Blob Storage backend\n* **Minimal OS and/or Kernel Version**: Reproduced on Windows\n* **Minimal Broker Client Version**: Not relevant\n* **Minimal Result Backend Client Version**: Azure Storage Blob client\n\n### Python Packages\n\n<!-- Please fill the contents of pip freeze below -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>pip freeze</code> Output:</b></summary>\n<p>\n\n```\nPlease replace this with the output of `pip freeze` from the reproduction environment.\n```\n\n</p>\n</details>\n\n### Other Dependencies\n\n<!--\nPlease provide system dependencies, configuration files\nand other dependency information if applicable\n-->\n\n<details>\n<p>\n\nAzure Blob Storage backend configuration is required. A live Azure account is not required to reproduce the redaction issue because the problem occurs while sanitizing the connection-string value.\n\n</p>\n</details>\n\n## Minimally Reproducible Test Case\n\n<!--\nPlease provide a reproducible test case.\nRefer to the Reporting Bugs section in our contribution guide.\n\nWe prefer submitting test cases in the form of a PR to our integration test suite.\nIf you can provide one, please mention the PR number below.\nIf not, please attach the most minimal code example required to reproduce the issue below.\nIf the test case is too large, please include a link to a gist or a repository below.\n\nAlternatively, the pytest-celery plugin can be used to create standalone reproduction scripts\nthat can be added to this report. See the pytest-celery documentation for more information at\npytest-celery.readthedocs.io\n-->\n\n<details>\n<p>\n\n```python\nfrom celery import Celery\nfrom celery.app.utils import sanitize_url\n\nbackend = (\n    \"azureblockblob://\"\n    \"DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;\"\n    \"AccountName=acct;\"\n    \"AccountKey=SECRET==;\"\n    \"EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net\"\n)\n\nprint(sanitize_url(backend))\n```\n\nThe current implementation returns the connection string with `AccountKey=SECRET==` unchanged.\n\nThe same value can reach Celery's diagnostic/configuration output through the bug-report path:\n\n```text\ncelery -A proj report\n```\n\nWhen an Azure Block Blob result backend is configured, the generated report can contain the storage account key in plaintext.\n\nA representative connection string is:\n\n```text\nazureblockblob://DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=acct;AccountKey=SECRET==;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net\n```\n\nNo real credential should be used when reproducing or reporting this issue.\n\n</p>\n</details>\n\n# Expected Behavior\n\n<!-- Describe in detail what you expect to happen -->\n\nSensitive credentials contained in Azure Block Blob connection strings should be redacted anywhere Celery sanitizes configuration values or generates diagnostic output.\n\nIn particular, `celery report` should not expose values such as:\n\n```text\nAccountKey=SECRET==\n```\n\nor:\n\n```text\nSharedAccessSignature=...\n```\n\nThe redaction behavior should be consistent with the existing redaction performed by `AzureBlockBlobBackend.as_uri()`.\n\n# Actual Behavior\n\n<!--\nDescribe in detail what actually happened.\nPlease include a backtrace and surround it with triple backticks (```).\nIn addition, include the Celery daemon logs, the broker logs,\nthe result backend logs and system logs below if they will help us debug\nthe issue.\n-->\n\n`sanitize_url()` does not redact credentials contained in Azure Blob Storage connection strings.\n\nThe current sanitization logic handles credentials represented in the URL authority portion, such as:\n\n```text\nredis://:password@host\n```\n\nHowever, Azure Block Blob credentials are embedded directly in the connection string:\n\n```text\nazureblockblob://DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=acct;AccountKey=SECRET==;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net\n```\n\nBecause there is no `user:password@host` component, the Azure connection string passes through `sanitize_url()` without the `AccountKey` being redacted.\n\nThis affects the configuration/diagnostic path used by `bugreport()` and therefore `celery report`.\n\nFor example, the resulting report can contain:\n\n```text\nresult_backend: azureblockblob://DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=acct;AccountKey=SECRET==;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net\n```\n\nThe credential can therefore be exposed if a user copies the output of `celery report` into a public bug report.\n\nThere is a related existing fix in #10620 where `AzureBlockBlobBackend.as_uri()` redacts Azure credentials. However, the configuration-level sanitization path does not use the same redaction logic, so the credentials can still be exposed through `celery report` and other paths based on `sanitize_url()`.\n\nThe issue also applies to Azure connection strings containing `SharedAccessSignature`.\n\nA possible fix would be to share the Azure connection-string redaction logic between `sanitize_url()` and `AzureBlockBlobBackend.as_uri()` so that both paths consistently protect the same sensitive fields.",
